module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Cover.Open
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Functorial
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect.SupportClosedSubset.ExtendedAlternatingCech

/-!
# Base change of the closed subscheme cut out by global equations

Let `g : X' ⟶ X` be a morphism of schemes and let `f₁, …, f_c ∈ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)`.  Put
`f'ᵢ = g^♯(fᵢ) ∈ Γ(X', 𝒪_{X'})` and let `Z ⊆ X`, resp. `Z' ⊆ X'`, be the closed subscheme cut
out by `f₁, …, f_c`, resp. `f'₁, …, f'_c`.  This file proves the assertion that opens the
setting of [Stacks, Tag 0G7U]: `Z' = Z ×_X X'`, in the strong form that the canonically induced
morphism `h : Z' ⟶ Z` makes

```
Z' --h--> Z
|         |
i'        i
v         v
X' --g--> X
```

a pullback square of schemes, so that `h` *is* the base change of `i` along `g`.  The file also
records the compatibility of the principal-open intersections of Tag 0G7I with pullback,
`g ⁻¹ᵁ U_{i₀…i_p} = U'_{i₀…i_p}`, which is what makes the two extended alternating Čech
complexes of Tag 0G7U comparable at all.

## Main results

* `Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_ofIdealTop`: the inverse image of the ideal sheaf generated by an
  ideal of global sections is the ideal sheaf generated by the image of that ideal under `g^♯`.
  This holds for an arbitrary morphism of schemes; Mathlib computes the inverse image of an
  ideal sheaf only for an open immersion
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_comap_of_isOpenImmersion`) and
  `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_of_isAffineHom` only for an affine morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech.isPullback_equationsClosedSubscheme`: the square
  displayed above is a pullback square, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech.equationsClosedSubschemePullbackIso`: the
  resulting identification `Z' ≅ Z ×_X X'`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech.range_equationsClosedSubschemeι_pullback`: on
  underlying sets, `Z'` is the inverse image of `Z`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech.preimage_iInf`: inverse image commutes with finite
  intersections of opens, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech.equationsOpen_pullback`: the principal-open
  intersection of the pulled-back equations is the inverse image of that of the equations.  The
  same statement for the `equationsOpen` of `Stacks.Perfect.ExtendedAlternatingCech` — the same
  definition in the other of the two namespaces that carry it — is
  `Stacks.Perfect.CechBaseChange.equationsOpen_pullback`, which is the one the Čech complex of
  `CechBaseChange.lean` is built from.

## Implementation notes

The closed subscheme of Tag 0G7I is `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (equationsIdeal f)`, the
ideal sheaf generated by the span of the equations.  Everything therefore reduces to the
behaviour of `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop` under `Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap`, and from
there to one statement: a global section lying in `I` pulls back to zero on the closed
subscheme of `ofIdealTop I` (`Stacks.IdealSheaf.appTop_subschemeι_ofIdealTop_eq_zero`).  That
one is affine-local — on an affine open `U` the ideal of `ofIdealTop I` is the image of `I`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_glueDataObjι_appTop` says exactly that this image
is killed — and is glued with `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.zero_of_zero_cover` along the affine
cover `Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeCover`.  The two inclusions of
`Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_ofIdealTop` then come out formally: the harder one from the Galois
connection `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_map_iff_comap_le`, which turns a bound on
the inverse image into a vanishing statement on the direct image, and the easier one from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_fst_of_isClosedImmersion` together with the
pullback square's own commutativity.

The pullback square itself is then
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_of_isClosedImmersion`, whose hypothesis is precisely the equality
of ideal sheaves just proved.

## Where the rest of Tag 0G7U lives

This file carries only the setting's assertion `Z' = Z ×_X X'`.  The remark's two commutative
diagrams, and the inputs they rest on, are elsewhere:

* The canonical comparison `L(g|_{Z'})^* R𝓗_Z(K) ⟶ R𝓗_{Z'}(Lg^*K)` of [Stacks, Tag 0G78] — the
  top horizontal arrow of the first diagram and the spine of the second — **is available**, in
  `StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Cohomology.SupportedComplexes.SupportedSectionsDerivedPullback`:
  `Stacks.Cohomology.SupportedComplexes.supportedPullbackMap`, together with the adjunction
  equation characterising it (`supportedPullbackMap_mate`), its uniqueness
  (`supportedPullbackMap_unique`), the invertibility of the base-change transformation of
  [Stacks, Tag 08HY] in this case (`isIso_supportedPullbackBaseChangeMap`), and the preservation
  of cohomological support by derived pullback (`cohomologySupportedOn_derivedPullback`).  The
  closed subset `Z' = g^{-1}(Z)` and the restricted morphism `g|_{Z'}` are
  `closedSubsetPreimage` and `closedSubsetRestriction` there.
* The comparison `g^*ℱ^• ⟶ (ℱ')^•` of the two extended alternating Čech complexes — the
  identification `(ℱ')^• = g^*ℱ^•` the remark asserts — **is available**, in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Perfect.SupportClosedSubset.CechBaseChange`:
  `Stacks.Perfect.CechBaseChange.cplxBaseChange` and its extension by zero to the `ℤ`-grading
  `extendBaseChange`, built termwise from
  `Stacks.Perfect.OpenPushRestrictBaseChange.openBaseChange` and the compatibility of the index
  opens `Stacks.Perfect.CechBaseChange.equationsOpen_pullback`.
* The SECOND of the remark's two diagrams — the derived one, which the remark states "without
  assuming `ℱ` is quasi-coherent" — **is proved**:
  `Stacks.Perfect.SupportedDerivedBaseChange.derivedBaseChangeSquare` for every lower horizontal
  arrow and down arrow compatible with the augmentations of [Stacks, Tag 0G7L], and
  `Stacks.Perfect.CechDerivedBaseChange.derivedBaseChangeSquare_cech` for the remark's own two
  arrows, which is where the `@[stacks 0G7U]` attribute for that diagram sits.
* The FIRST of the remark's two diagrams — the quasi-coherent one, on the cohomology sheaves in
  degree `c`, with the class maps `c_{f₁,…,f_c}` of [Stacks, Tag 0G7Q] as its vertical arrows —
  **is proved**:
  `Stacks.Perfect.CechDegreeCBaseChange.supportedFractionSource_baseChange`, where the
  `@[stacks 0G7U]` attribute for that diagram sits, with its top arrow
  `Stacks.Perfect.CechDegreeCBaseChange.degreeCBaseChange`.  The compatibility of the
  construction of [Stacks, Tag 0G7Q] with pullbacks that the source invokes for it is
  `Stacks.Perfect.CechFractionBaseChange.cplxBaseChange_comp_fracTermTop`.
* Along an **open immersion** the identification of the complexes is available by restriction
  rather than by pullback as well, in `CechComplexBaseChange.lean`:
  `Stacks.Perfect.PushforwardRestrict.restrictData` exhibits the restriction to an open of a
  complex satisfying the specification of Tag 0G7I as one for the restricted equations, and
  `…restrictComplexIso` is the resulting isomorphism with any other such complex, on the
  termwise comparison `…restrictRestrictedModuleNatIso` of `CechTermBaseChange.lean`.  The
  termwise comparison of the direct images `(U_{i₀…i_p} → X)_*(ℱ|_{U_{i₀…i_p}})` is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech.pullbackRestrictedModuleMap` of
  `OpenDirectImagePullback.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G7U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G7U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G7I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G7I)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.IdealSheaf

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The global sections of an open subscheme, read on the ambient scheme, are the restrictions
of the ambient global sections. -/
public theorem ι_appTop_comp_topIso_hom (V : X.Opens) :
    V.ι.appTop ≫ V.topIso.hom = X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V))).op := by
  change X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (x := V.ι ''ᵁ ⊤) le_top).op ≫
      X.presheaf.map (eqToHom V.ι_image_top.symm).op = _
  rw [← Functor.map_comp]
  congr 1

/-- A global section of `X` belonging to `I` pulls back to zero on the closed subscheme cut out
by the ideal sheaf generated by `I`. -/
public theorem appTop_subschemeι_ofIdealTop_eq_zero (I : Ideal Γ(X, ⊤)) {a : Γ(X, ⊤)}
    (ha : a ∈ I) :
    ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).subschemeι.appTop).hom a = 0 := by
  have key : ∀ V : X.affineOpens,
      (((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).subschemeCover.f V ≫
        (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).subschemeι).appTop).hom a = 0 := by
    intro V
    have h3 : (V.1.topIso.hom).hom ((V.1.ι.appTop).hom a) =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top (a := V.1))).op).hom a := by
      rw [← CommRingCat.comp_apply, ι_appTop_comp_topIso_hom]
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeCover_map_subschemeι, Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop]
    change (((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).glueDataObjι V).appTop).hom
      ((V.1.ι.appTop).hom a) = 0
    rw [← RingHom.mem_ker, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_glueDataObjι_appTop,
      Ideal.mem_comap, h3, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha
  refine Scheme.zero_of_zero_cover _
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).subschemeCover.openCover ?_
  intro U
  have h := key U
  rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop] at h
  exact h

/-- The ideal sheaf generated by an ideal `I` of global sections is contained in the kernel of
`φ` as soon as every element of `I` pulls back to zero along `φ`. -/
public theorem ofIdealTop_le_ker {W : Scheme.{u}} (φ : W ⟶ X) (I : Ideal Γ(X, ⊤))
    (h : ∀ a ∈ I, (φ.appTop).hom a = 0) :
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I ≤ φ.ker := by
  refine Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_ofIdeals_iff.mpr fun U => ?_
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop_ideal, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
  intro a ha
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker]
  have hnat := φ.naturality (U := U.1) (U' := ⊤) (homOfLE (le_top (a := U.1))).op
  have h1 := congrArg (fun ψ : Γ(X, ⊤) ⟶ _ => (CommRingCat.Hom.hom ψ) a) hnat
  simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp, RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply] at h1
  refine h1.trans ?_
  exact (congrArg _ (h a ha)).trans (map_zero _)

/-- **The inverse image of an ideal sheaf generated by global sections.** For an arbitrary
morphism of schemes `g : X ⟶ Y`, the inverse image of the ideal sheaf generated by an ideal `I`
of `Γ(Y, 𝒪_Y)` is the ideal sheaf generated by the image of `I` under `g^♯`. -/
public theorem comap_ofIdealTop (g : X ⟶ Y) (I : Ideal Γ(Y, ⊤)) :
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).comap g =
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (Ideal.map g.appTop.hom I) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_map_iff_comap_le]
    refine ofIdealTop_le_ker _ _ fun a ha => ?_
    show (((Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
      (Ideal.map g.appTop.hom I)).subschemeι ≫ g).appTop).hom a = 0
    rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, CommRingCat.comp_apply]
    exact appTop_subschemeι_ofIdealTop_eq_zero _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)
  · have hcomap : (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).comap g =
        (pullback.fst g (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop I).subschemeι).ker := by
      rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_fst_of_isClosedImmersion,
        Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι]
    rw [hcomap]
    refine ofIdealTop_le_ker _ _ fun b hb => ?_
    rw [← RingHom.mem_ker]
    refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr (fun a ha => ?_) hb
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, RingHom.mem_ker, ← CommRingCat.comp_apply,
      ← Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop, pullback.condition, Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop,
      CommRingCat.comp_apply]
    exact (congrArg _ (appTop_subschemeι_ofIdealTop_eq_zero I ha)).trans (map_zero _)

end Stacks.IdealSheaf

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech

variable {X X' : Scheme.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ X) {c : ℕ} (f : Fin c → Γ(X, ⊤))

/-- The closed immersion of the closed subscheme cut out by the equations. -/
public def equationsClosedSubschemeι : equationsClosedSubscheme f ⟶ X :=
  (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (equationsIdeal f)).subschemeι

/-- The inclusion of the closed subscheme cut out by the equations is a closed immersion. -/
public instance : IsClosedImmersion (equationsClosedSubschemeι f) :=
  inferInstanceAs
    (IsClosedImmersion (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (equationsIdeal f)).subschemeι)

/-- The ideal generated by the pulled-back equations is the image of the ideal generated by the
equations. -/
public theorem equationsIdeal_pullback :
    equationsIdeal (fun j => g.appTop (f j)) = Ideal.map g.appTop.hom (equationsIdeal f) := by
  simp only [equationsIdeal, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  rfl

/-- Taking inverse images commutes with finite intersections of opens. -/
public theorem preimage_iInf {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (V : ι → X.Opens) :
    g ⁻¹ᵁ (⨅ k, V k) = ⨅ k, g ⁻¹ᵁ (V k) := by
  apply Opens.ext
  simp [Opens.coe_iInf, Set.preimage_iInter]

/-- The principal-open intersection of the pulled-back equations is the inverse image of the
principal-open intersection of the equations. -/
public theorem equationsOpen_pullback (p : ℕ) (s : CechCochains.OrdIndex (I := Fin c) p) :
    g ⁻¹ᵁ equationsOpen f p s = equationsOpen (fun j => g.appTop (f j)) p s := by
  simp only [equationsOpen, preimage_iInf]
  exact iInf_congr fun k => Scheme.preimage_basicOpen g _

/-- The inverse image of the ideal sheaf cut out by the equations is the ideal sheaf cut out by
the pulled-back equations. -/
public theorem comap_equationsIdealSheaf :
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (equationsIdeal f)).comap g =
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (equationsIdeal (fun j => g.appTop (f j))) := by
  rw [Stacks.IdealSheaf.comap_ofIdealTop, equationsIdeal_pullback]

/-- The morphism `h : Z' ⟶ Z` induced by `g` between the closed subschemes cut out by the
pulled-back equations and by the equations. -/
public def equationsClosedSubschemeBaseChange :
    equationsClosedSubscheme (fun j => g.appTop (f j)) ⟶ equationsClosedSubscheme f :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap _ _ g
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.le_map_iff_comap_le.mpr (comap_equationsIdealSheaf g f).le)

/-- The square `h ≫ i = i' ≫ g` of [Stacks, Tag 0G7U] commutes. -/
public theorem equationsClosedSubschemeBaseChange_comp :
    equationsClosedSubschemeBaseChange g f ≫ equationsClosedSubschemeι f =
      equationsClosedSubschemeι (fun j => g.appTop (f j)) ≫ g :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeMap_subschemeι _ _ _ _

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0G7U**, the assertion `Z' = Z ×_X X'` of the setting: the closed
subscheme cut out by the pulled-back equations `f'ᵢ = g^♯(fᵢ)` is the base change along `g` of
the closed subscheme cut out by `f₁, …, f_c`, the induced morphism of schemes being
`equationsClosedSubschemeBaseChange`.

The set-theoretic form of the same assertion, which is the shape [Stacks, Tag 0G78] and hence
the remark's diagrams are stated at, is
`Stacks.Perfect.SupportedDerivedBaseChange.equationsClosedSet_pullback`. -/
@[stacks 0G7U "Z' = Z ×_X X' of the setting, as a pullback square of schemes"]
public theorem isPullback_equationsClosedSubscheme :
    IsPullback (equationsClosedSubschemeι (fun j => g.appTop (f j)))
      (equationsClosedSubschemeBaseChange g f) g (equationsClosedSubschemeι f) := by
  refine isPullback_of_isClosedImmersion _ _ _ _
    (equationsClosedSubschemeBaseChange_comp g f).symm ?_
  change (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (equationsIdeal f)).subschemeι.ker.comap g = _
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι]
  change _ = (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
    (equationsIdeal (fun j => g.appTop (f j)))).subschemeι.ker
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι]
  exact comap_equationsIdealSheaf g f

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0G7U**, the identification `Z' = Z ×_X X'` of the setting, as an
isomorphism of schemes. -/
@[stacks 0G7U "the identification Z' ≅ Z ×_X X' of the setting"]
public def equationsClosedSubschemePullbackIso :
    equationsClosedSubscheme (fun j => g.appTop (f j)) ≅
      pullback g (equationsClosedSubschemeι f) :=
  (isPullback_equationsClosedSubscheme g f).isoPullback

/-- The underlying closed set of `Z'` is the inverse image of the underlying closed set of
`Z`. -/
public theorem range_equationsClosedSubschemeι_pullback :
    Set.range (equationsClosedSubschemeι (fun j => g.appTop (f j))) =
      g ⁻¹' Set.range (equationsClosedSubschemeι f) := by
  change Set.range (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop
    (equationsIdeal (fun j => g.appTop (f j)))).subschemeι = _
  rw [← comap_equationsIdealSheaf g f, Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  change _ = g ⁻¹' Set.range (Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop (equationsIdeal f)).subschemeι
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
  rfl

end AlgebraicGeometry.ExtendedAlternatingCech

end
